 {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. Before retrying, I'll check whether it was actually created, so I don't open a duplicate page.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KzYFm2KiTa4HykBuhTHdw6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It reports healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release with a healthy production history. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both unhealthy. Because v2.3.0 was previously healthy in production, the change-manager approval requirement did not apply.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error. That left the service mixed, with us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1. I retried the same rollback, and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001. The create call timed out, so I checked the incident list before anything else. It showed the incident had been created, so I did not open a duplicate. The summary covers the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the follow-up items.\n\nFollow-up for the team: find out why v2.3.1 failed health checks, and why the orchestrator halted the first rollback. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it is fixed.", "type": "text"}]}]}